      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Cloud Provider**\n\nI've decided to use Google Cloud Pub/Sub and am getting started on a Python script, `consume_event.py`, that retrieves a single message from a managed subscription. The goal is now to write the script, but I'm focusing on the provider setup.\n\n\n**Defining the Consumption Process**\n\nI'm now creating the Python file, `consume_event.py`, specifically using the Google Cloud Pub/Sub library, `google-cloud-pubsub`. The code will import `pubsub_v1` from `google.cloud` and define a function that consumes a single message. I plan to use `SubscriberClient` to connect to Pub/Sub, specifying a project and subscription ID. I'll call `subscribe` and `pull` (or a similar method) to retrieve and then acknowledge the received message.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865094498,
          "start": 1789865091563
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc45e1eb0015nDTOcNKgRmJhH",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc45db42001cMyL6CYIrGefV0",
      "session_id": "ses_f43ba24cbffeNj91dRAQF8zAZ6",
      "time_created": 1789865091563,
      "time_updated": 1789865094499
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "MMTTmRXei10t40ZA",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import pubsub_v1\nimport os\n\ndef consume_message(project_id: str, subscription_id: str):\n    \"\"\"Consumes one message from a Pub/Sub subscription.\"\"\"\n    \n    subscriber = pubsub_v1.SubscriberClient()\n    subscription_path = subscriber.subscription_path(project_id, subscription_id)\n\n    def callback(message: pubsub_v1.types.PubsubMessage):\n        print(f\"Received message: {message.data.decode(\"utf-8\")}\")\n        message.ack()\n\n    streaming_pull_future = subscriber.subscribe(subscription_path, callback=callback)\n    print(f\"Listening for messages on {subscription_path}...\")\n\n    # Wrap subscriber in a 'with' block to automatically call close() when done.\n    with subscriber:\n        try:\n            # When `timeout` is not set, result() will block indefinitely to await messages\n            streaming_pull_future.result(timeout=30)\n        except TimeoutError:\n            streaming_pull_future.cancel()  # Trigger the shutdown.\n            streaming_pull_future.result()  # Block until the shutdown is complete.\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Replace with your Google Cloud Project ID and Subscription ID\n    project_id = os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT\")\n    subscription_id = os.environ.get(\"PUBSUB_SUBSCRIPTION_ID\")\n\n    if not project_id or not subscription_id:\n        print(\"Please set the GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT and PUBSUB_SUBSCRIPTION_ID environment variables.\")\n    else:\n        consume_message(project_id, subscription_id)\n",
            "filePath": "consume_event.py"
          },
